I checked her level: 10. I created a lot of monsters, but it didn't
change. And about a quarter of the monsters were ignored by her.
Probably too high level.

So, I was having serious doubts about her survivability. After some
consideration, I zapped her again, and I got: a baby gray dragon! OK!
After summoning one (whimpy) monster, it turned into a grown Gray
Dragon (lvl 16). Now that's more like it!

Not the very best pet, but immune to most magic and very survivable, I
think.

Can trappers or purple worms digest such a big creature? If they can,
I'll genocide them.

And I know about system shock, but you have to do something. And it's
probably easily remedied by sacrificing a lot of stuff. But I'm glad
it turned out like it did.


Btw, if you get a wizard through the early game, they're by far the
most powerful class in my opinion. Especially with create monster and
polymorph on 0%, whatever you want mostly takes time. And finger of
death and magic missile rule in combat, when you have just about
unlimited spell points. Even the castle and valley of death are a
piece of cake.

Having said that, I pray to the NRNG: "I'll be your slave, don't YASD
me, please!"

Now to think about naming it. How can I see if my pet dragon is male
or female? A stethoscope doesn't show that, and the message log
doesn't, either. Or I could think of an unisexual name.



